  "forward":{"entry_point":"ignis_wsp::property_solids_v2::State::advance_refined","version":"property-solids-law-review-v2.1","profile":"strict_no_fitting"},
  "notes":"New source-root candidate informed by synthetic/physics review and prior unregistered author packet; not a clean-room W0. Original physical literals inherited unchanged. New numerical method performs whole-interval n/2n/4n split refinement with explicit caller temperature/mass estimator tolerances, contraction ceiling and work limits. TemporalReceipt reports observed-asymptotic estimates, never rigorous exact-flow error bounds; spatial error and physical uncertainty remain separate. The explicitly separate advance_checked mode only enforces numerical split-path domains and arithmetic ledgers. Both modes reject boundary-property invalidity at initial/heated/final exposed temperatures atomically. Solid matrix, pyrolysis and gas-phase limitations of predecessor remain; no luminous-front or quench closure was added. The three local source aliases describing prior work/review are not fabricated app EvaluationId/ReleaseId records. Coordinator owns adapter and immutable release assembly."
